  "term": "linguistic universal",
  "definition": "A linguistic universal is a pattern or property that appears across many or all human languages. In this source, such universals are described as possibly arising either from an innate universal grammar or from shared cognitive or perceptual biases, with cultural history also shaping how strongly the universal pattern appears.",
